# SPECTRA - .gitattributes
#
# Status: session one. This file is the thing being delivered.
#
# Two specification fragments are merged here and both are normative:
#   Part II section 73.8    - Linguist rules and the anti-inflation ban
#   Part II section 74.10.5 - line endings, gate G-WIN-002 (this file must
#                             match the committed golden copy byte for byte)
#
# ANTI-INFLATION STATEMENT (Part II section 73.8, hard ban).
# Nothing in this file is miscategorised to add a row to, or grow a row in, the
# GitHub language bar. `linguist-language=` appears exactly once below and only
# to correct a genuine misdetection, with a one-line comment saying which.
# Renaming fixtures to a source extension, declaring configuration as code,
# tagging generated output as authored, or splitting one component across
# extensions to add a bar row is inflation and fails `make polyglot-audit` with
# LINGUIST_OVERRIDE_UNJUSTIFIED or BAR_INFLATION. Generated code, vendored
# code, fixtures and compiled wasm are counted at zero, on purpose.

# ===========================================================================
# 1. Baseline: normalise every text file to LF in the working tree and the index
# ===========================================================================
* text=auto eol=lf

# ===========================================================================
# 2. Explicit LF for every text type the repository will contain
#    (Part II section 74.10.5; the roster is Part II sections 73.1-73.2.)
#    Declared ahead of the source directories existing: a file that appears
#    later must not be able to arrive with CRLF.
# ===========================================================================

